## AGENT SELECTION QUICK REFERENCE

**Purpose**: Fast lookup for which agent handles which activity

**Pattern**: Activity → Agent → Skills Needed → Starting Line

### Agent Selection Decision Tree

```
QUESTION: What work needs to be done?

IF: Designing interface
  → Agent 1: Interface Architect Agent (Line 135)
  → Skills: Interface Designer, Canonical Type Reuse
  → Entry: Interface Proposal Workflow (Line 229)

IF: Reviewing for operations/security/reliability
  → Agent 2: Operational Review Agent (Line 287)
  → Skills: Operational review skills (see Agent 2 section)
  → Entry: Detailed Review Checklist (Line 359)

IF: Implementing approved interface
  → Agent 3: Construct Implementation Agent (Line 551)
  → Skills: CDK Construct Implementation, Testing, Coding Conventions
  → Entry: Complete Development Lifecycle (Line 630)

IF: Modifying module structure
  → Agent 1 OR Agent 3 (depending on phase)
  → Skills: Module Layout Enforcer
  → Entry: Agent 1 (design phase) or Agent 3 (implementation phase)

IF: Testing construct
  → Agent 3: Construct Implementation Agent
  → Skills: Testing
  → Entry: Phase 4: Testing (Line ~750)

IF: Creating PR
  → Agent 3: Construct Implementation Agent
  → Entry: Phase 7: Pull Request Creation (Line ~950)

IF: Resolving standards conflict
  → Agent 2: Operational Review Agent
  → Entry: Conflict Resolution Pattern (Line 456)
```

