### Workflow Entry Points by Frequency

**Pattern**: Workflow → Agent → Starting Line

| Workflow | Agent | Starting Line | When to Use |
|----------|-------|---------------|-------------|
| Complete Development Lifecycle | Agent 3 | Line 630 | Most common: implementing new construct |
| Interface Proposal | Agent 1 | Line 229 | Before any implementation (MANDATORY) |
| Detailed Review Checklist | Agent 2 | Line 359 | After implementation, before PR |
| Conflict Resolution | Agent 2 | Line 456 | When standards conflict or ambiguity exists |
| Testing Workflow | Agent 3 | Line ~750 | Part of Complete Development Lifecycle |
| PR Creation | Agent 3 | Line ~950 | After all quality gates pass |

### Agent Collaboration Patterns

**Pattern**: Sequence → Handoff Point

```
PATTERN 1: New Construct (Full Lifecycle)
Agent 1 (Interface Design)
  → Output: Approved interface
  → Handoff to: Agent 3
Agent 3 (Implementation + Testing)
  → Output: Implemented construct + tests passing
  → Handoff to: Agent 2
Agent 2 (Operational Review)
  → Output: Review findings + approval
  → Handoff to: Agent 3
Agent 3 (PR Creation)
  → Output: Pull request created

PATTERN 2: Interface Evolution
Agent 1 (Interface Design - Evolution Mode)
  → Output: Updated interface + migration path
  → Handoff to: Agent 3
Agent 3 (Update Implementation + Tests)
  → Output: Updated construct + passing tests
  → Handoff to: Agent 2
Agent 2 (Change Safety Review)
  → Output: Safety assessment + approval

PATTERN 3: Standards Conflict Resolution
Agent 2 (Conflict Resolution Pattern)
  → Output: Resolved approach + documentation
  → Handoff to: Original agent to continue work
```

### Common Questions → Answers

**Pattern**: Question → Answer → Line Reference

| Question | Answer | Line Reference |
|----------|--------|----------------|
| Which agent designs interfaces? | Agent 1: Interface Architect | Line 135 |
| Which agent implements constructs? | Agent 3: Construct Implementation | Line 551 |
| Which agent reviews for operations? | Agent 2: Operational Review | Line 287 |
| What skills are implemented? | 5 skills (see Quick Skill Lookup above) | - |
| Where are standards? | `docs/standards/**` | See Documentation section |
| Where are skills? | `docs/skills/**` | Line 67 |
| How do I resolve conflicts? | Agent 2 Conflict Resolution Pattern | Line 456 |
| Can agents modify interfaces? | NO - Human approval required | See Agent 1 Approval Gate |

### Critical Rules (All Agents MUST Follow)

**Pattern**: Rule → Enforcement

1. **Constitutional Authority**: CLAUDE.md overrides AGENTS.md in conflicts
2. **Fail-Closed**: If information missing → STOP and ASK
3. **No Pre-emption**: Complete requested task → STOP → OFFER suggestions → WAIT
4. **Skill Constraints**: Agents may only invoke skills assigned to them
5. **Approval Gates**: Human approval required before modifying interfaces, deploying to AWS, breaking changes
6. **Repository Style**: All agents MUST follow Repository Style & Consistency Rules (Line 143)
7. **Quality Gates**: Never skip build, lint, test, or standards compliance gates

