#### Pre-PR Checklist

Before creating PR, Agent 3 MUST verify ALL of the following:

**Planning**
- [ ] Requirements clarified with user
- [ ] Reviewed relevant `docs/standards/` documentation
- [ ] Created feature branch

**Development**
- [ ] Construct created following layer-specific patterns
- [ ] Types defined in `types.ts`
- [ ] Exports added to `src/index.ts`
- [ ] TSDoc with `@example` tags added
- [ ] Reviewed against `docs/standards/common/anti-patterns.md`
- [ ] No anti-patterns present

**Testing (Optimized Workflow)**
- [ ] Unit tests created with 85%+ coverage
- [ ] **Performance optimizations applied**:
    - [ ] Minimized `Template.fromStack()` calls (use `beforeAll()`)
    - [ ] Lambda bundling ≤ 3 per test file (hard cap)
    - [ ] Test file duration benchmarked
    - [ ] Test file completes in < 30 seconds (< 10 seconds target)
    - [ ] If > 30 seconds, added to `.projen/jest-test-sequencer.js`
- [ ] **Ran construct tests FIRST**: `npx jest src/test/{module}`
- [ ] All construct tests pass [VERIFIED]
- [ ] Jest integration test created
- [ ] **Ran integration tests**: `npx jest --config src/integration/jest.config.js --testPathPattern={module}`
- [ ] All integration tests pass ✅
- [ ] **ONLY then ran full build**: `npx projen build`
- [ ] Build passes ✅

**Quality**
- [ ] `npx projen eslint` passes with no new errors
- [ ] Code reviewed against best practices
- [ ] Agent 2 review checklist completed

**Integration Stack Validation** (Required)
- [ ] User authenticated: `aws sso login --profile <profile>`
- [ ] Credentials verified: `aws sts get-caller-identity --profile <profile>`
- [ ] Synthesized stack: `npx cdk synth --app "..."`
- [ ] Reviewed CloudFormation template in `cdk.out/`
- [ ] Deployed stack: `npx cdk deploy --app "..." --profile <profile>`
- [ ] Stack reached CREATE_COMPLETE status
- [ ] User validated resources in AWS Console
- [ ] Security settings verified (encryption, policies, logging, etc.)
- [ ] Destroyed stack: `npx cdk destroy --app "..." --profile <profile> --force`
- [ ] Stack reached DELETE_COMPLETE status
- [ ] User verified no orphaned resources

**Pull Request**
- [ ] Branch pushed to remote
- [ ] PR created with complete template
- [ ] User notified to add Jira ticket
- [ ] User notified to add label (see `docs/standards/sdlc/pull-request.md`)
- [ ] User notified to review and approve

---

#### Integration Testing Patterns

**Two types of integration tests:**

**1. Jest Integration Tests** (`*.integration.test.ts`)

- **Purpose**: Test construct CloudFormation templates locally without AWS deployment
- **When**: Run automatically in CI/CD, no AWS credentials required
- **Location**: `src/integration/{service}/{construct-name}.integration.test.ts`
- **Speed**: Fast (< 1 minute typically)

**Commands**:
```bash
# Run all integration tests
npx jest --config src/integration/jest.config.js

# Run specific service
npx jest --config src/integration/jest.config.js --testPathPattern={service}
```

**What to test**:
- CloudFormation template structure
- Resource properties and configurations
- Resource counts
- Outputs
- Tags and metadata

**2. CDK Integration Tests** (`integ.*.ts`)

- **Purpose**: Deploy actual resources to AWS for validation
- **When**: Before PR creation, requires AWS authentication
- **Location**: `src/integration/{service}/integ.{construct-name}.ts`
- **Speed**: Slow (5-15 minutes typically for deploy + destroy)
- **Requirements**: AWS SSO, user-provided credentials

**Commands**:
```bash
# User authenticates first (user responsibility)
aws sso login --profile <profile>

# Agent can run these with user-provided profile:
npx cdk synth --app "npx ts-node src/integration/{service}/integ.{construct-name}.ts"
npx cdk deploy --app "..." --profile <profile>
npx cdk destroy --app "..." --profile <profile> --force
```

**What to validate**:
- Actual AWS resource creation
- Security configurations (encryption, access controls)
- Network configurations
- IAM policies and roles
- Resource interdependencies
- Stack outputs
- Clean deletion (no orphaned resources)

**Integration Test Requirements**:
- Use `RemovalPolicy.DESTROY` for all resources
- Include `CfnOutput` for validation points
- Test multiple scenarios when applicable
- Clean up properly in `cdk destroy`

---

## Agent Collaboration Model

Default flow:

1. **Interface Architect Agent** (Agent 1)
2. **Operational Review Agent** (Agent 2)
3. **Construct Implementation Agent** (Agent 3)
4. Human approval
5. Release & evolution planning

Agents may not skip steps without explicit human approval.
Agents must also comply with the Repository Style & Consistency Rules above.

---

## AWS Authentication Rules

**CRITICAL RULE**: AI agents CANNOT and MUST NOT attempt to authenticate to AWS.

### User Responsibilities

**User MUST**:
1. Authenticate via AWS SSO:
   ```bash
   aws sso login --profile <profile-name>
   ```

2. Verify credentials:
   ```bash
   aws sts get-caller-identity --profile <profile-name>
   ```

3. Provide profile name to agent when AWS operations are needed

4. Validate resources in AWS Console after deployment

5. Verify cleanup after `cdk destroy`

**Required Permission Set**: `te-claude-cdk-*`

### AI Agent Responsibilities

**Agent MUST**:
1. **Prompt user to authenticate** before any AWS operation
2. **Wait for user to provide profile name**
3. Construct CDK commands with user-provided profile
4. Execute `cdk synth`, `cdk deploy`, `cdk destroy` with proper profile
5. **Never attempt to log in to AWS**
6. **Never proceed with AWS operations without user-provided credentials**

### AWS Operation Workflow

**Step 1: Request Authentication**
```text
I need to perform AWS operations (deploy/test/validate).

Please authenticate with AWS SSO:
  aws sso login --profile <your-profile-name>

Then verify your credentials:
  aws sts get-caller-identity --profile <your-profile-name>

Once authenticated, please provide your profile name.

[WAIT FOR USER TO AUTHENTICATE AND PROVIDE PROFILE]
```

**Step 2: Execute with Profile**
```bash
# Agent can now run with user-provided profile
npx cdk synth --app "..."
npx cdk deploy --app "..." --profile <user-provided-profile>
npx cdk destroy --app "..." --profile <user-provided-profile> --force
```

**Step 3: User Validation**
- User validates resources in AWS Console
- User verifies cleanup completed
- User confirms no orphaned resources or unexpected costs

---

## Agent Tool Reference

Agents may use the following tools during construct development:

### Node/NPM Tools

```bash
nvm use                    # Switch to correct Node version (.nvmrc)
npm ci                     # Clean install dependencies
npx projen                 # Update project configuration
npx projen build           # Build and test (full cycle, slow)
npx projen test            # Run unit tests only
npx projen eslint          # Lint code
npx projen compile         # Compilation only
```

### Git Tools

```bash
git checkout -b <branch>   # Create feature/fix branch
git add .                  # Stage all changes
git commit -m "message"    # Commit with conventional message
git push -u origin <branch># Push branch to remote
git status                 # Check working directory status
```

**Conventional Commit Formats**:
- `feat(service): description` - New feature
- `fix(service): description` - Bug fix
- `docs(service): description` - Documentation only
- `refactor(service): description` - Code refactoring
- `test(service): description` - Test additions/changes
- `chore(service): description` - Maintenance tasks

### GitHub CLI Tools

```bash
gh pr create               # Create pull request
gh pr list                 # List all PRs
gh pr view                 # View PR details
gh pr status               # Check PR status
```

### AWS CLI Tools (User Responsibility - AI Cannot Authenticate)

```bash
# User must authenticate
aws sso login --profile <profile>

# User can verify credentials
aws sts get-caller-identity --profile <profile>

# Agent can help construct AWS CLI commands with user-provided profile
aws <service> <operation> --profile <profile>
```

**WARNING**: Agent must NEVER run `aws sso login`. This is user responsibility.

### CDK CLI Tools

```bash
# Synthesize CloudFormation template
npx cdk synth --app "npx ts-node src/integration/{service}/integ.{construct}.ts"

# Show changes (diff)
npx cdk diff --app "..." --profile <profile>

# Deploy stack (requires user authentication)
npx cdk deploy --app "..." --profile <profile>

# Destroy stack (requires user authentication)
npx cdk destroy --app "..." --profile <profile> --force

# List stacks
npx cdk list --app "..."
```

### Jest Testing Tools

```bash
# Run specific test file
npx jest src/test/{service}/{construct}.test.ts

# Run all tests in a directory
npx jest src/test/{service}/

# Run integration tests
npx jest --config src/integration/jest.config.js

# Run with pattern matching
npx jest --testPathPattern={pattern}

# Run with coverage
npx jest --coverage
```

### Tool Usage Guidelines

1. **Test locally first** - Use `npx jest` before `npx projen build` to iterate faster
2. **Minimize full builds** - Only run `npx projen build` when confident tests pass
3. **Use specific test commands** - Target specific test files for faster feedback
4. **Wait for user authentication** - Never attempt AWS operations without user credentials
5. **Verify before destroy** - Always confirm resources are validated before cleanup

---

## MCP Tool Usage (Future-Compatible)

Agents may use MCP tools only as allowed by `CLAUDE.md` and must obey module path conventions (e.g., `src/core/**` is pure capability only).

Expected future MCP capabilities include:

- File read/write
- CDK synth
- Test execution
- Interface validation

No destructive actions are permitted without approval.

---

## Fail-Closed Rule

If inputs are missing, ambiguous, or conflicting:

- STOP
- Ask for clarification
- Do NOT proceed

This rule overrides all others.
